A||||6||hugh||Drag race tips! Got any?||||5||
Z||000000||hugh||09-02-2001||08:01 AM||||I know lots of forum members drag race cars,bikes,rails,etc.Any tricks big or little that you use on the track that anyone else can use?One little thing I've used is to lock up the torque converter on my GN by putting a switch under my dash that connects the top right terminal to the top left terminal on my ALDL.When I connect them together the converter locks up as soon as it hits second gear.It won't lock up in first.This mod is good for a 10th or 2 in the 1/4 mile. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||rockcrawl||09-02-2001||08:12 AM||||Hey Hugh, I've got a tip. Don't fall asleep looking at the Ford Lightning in the right lane that's about to whoop your ass! When I saw him pull away, I figured it was time to go  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Sorry I can't provide any real tips.||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||09-02-2001||08:27 AM||||Hey Jon,Next time that Lightning is around we'll cream him with the 88,if that doesn't work,we'll bring out the big guns(GN).<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||09-02-2001||09:05 AM||||Yep. Use brakes at other end  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000004||Kasdan||09-02-2001||10:04 AM||||Seriously, hold brake, put car in neutral, rev motor to 6k, and when green light hits, power brake it!  <P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000005||hugh||09-02-2001||10:11 AM||||Kasdan,OUCH!<BR>  You mean break,not brake. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by hugh (edited 09-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bazooka||09-02-2001||11:30 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by hugh:<BR>[B]I know lots of forum members drag race cars,bikes,rails,etc.Any tricks big or little that you use on the track that anyone else can use?One little thing I've used is to lock up the torque converter on my GN by putting a switch under my dash that connects the top right terminal to the top left terminal on my ALDL.When I connect them together the converter locks up as soon as it hits second gear.It won't lock up in first.This mod is good for a 10th or 2 in the 1/4 mile.<BR>*****************************************<BR>Hugh,<BR>    If you have fuel injection(TPI or PFI) you can save ET time by Icing the plenum before runs. You can use a bag of regular ice or better yet dry ice. Caution here tho: some dragstrips don't allow icing in competition.  If you have carburetion, you can make a Cooling Can for the fuel line/carb inlet that is made up of coils of tubing inside of a coffee can that are cooled with reg ice or dry ice. <BR> <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html</A> <P>********************************************<P>||||reg||1
